hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15545","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ubaydillah ibn Thalabah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: I heard Mujammi ibn Jariyah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned al-Dajjal and said: The son of Maryam will kill him at the gate of Ludd."
"15546","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to us that he heard Ubaydillah ibn Thalabah al-Ansari narrating, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid al-Ansari, of Banu Amr ibn Awf, saying: I heard my uncle Mujammi ibn Jariyah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The son of Maryam will kill al-Masih al-Dajjal at the gate of Ludd."
"15547","Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydillah ibn Thalabah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his uncle Mujammi, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The son of Maryam will kill al-Masih al-Dajjal at the gate of Ludd."
"15548","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Ubaydillah ibn Thalabah al-Ansari, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Mujammi ibn Jariyah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The son of Maryam will kill al-Dajjal at the gate of Ludd, or beside Ludd."
"15549","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Mujammi ibn Yaqub narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying, from his uncle Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his uncle Mujammi ibn Jariyah al-Ansari, and he was one of the reciters who recited the Quran, he said: We witnessed al-Hudaybiyah, and when we turned back from it, people were making the camels flee. People said, some to others: What is with the people? They said: Revelation was sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So we went out with the people hastening until we found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon his mount at Kura al-Ghamim, and the people gathered to him, and he recited to them: Verily We have opened for you a clear opening. A man of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Messenger of Allah, and is it a victory? He said: Yes, by the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, it is indeed a victory. So Khaybar was divided among the people of al-Hudaybiyah, none was admitted with them in it except one who witnessed al-Hudaybiyah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided it into eighteen shares, and the army was one thousand five hundred, among them three hundred horsemen. So he gave the horseman two shares and gave the footman one share."
